import{_ as i,o as t,c as n,a2 as a}from"./chunks/framework.CqpfiAoK.js";const p=JSON.parse('{"title":"Entry 814 | Transcended Ones and Laws | The Democratic Procedure of Law Revision","description":"","frontmatter":{"title":"Entry 814 | Transcended Ones and Laws | The Democratic Procedure of Law Revision","no":814,"module":4,"tags":["Transcended One","Laws","Law Revision","Democratic Procedure","Myriad-Rank Republicanism"],"related":["03-Symbiotic-Civilization Charter","40-Symbiotic Constitution Outline","29-Symbiosis-Degree Assessment System"]},"headers":[],"relativePath":"en/0814_模块4-超脱者与法则-法则修订民主程序.md","filePath":"en/0814_模块4-超脱者与法则-法则修订民主程序.md"}'),o={name:"en/0814_模块4-超脱者与法则-法则修订民主程序.md"};function s(r,e,l,d,c,h){return t(),n("div",null,[...e[0]||(e[0]=[a('<h1 id="entry-814-transcended-ones-and-laws-the-democratic-procedure-of-law-revision" tabindex="-1">Entry 814 | Transcended Ones and Laws | The Democratic Procedure of Law Revision <a class="header-anchor" href="#entry-814-transcended-ones-and-laws-the-democratic-procedure-of-law-revision" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Entry 814 | Transcended Ones and Laws | The Democratic Procedure of Law Revision&quot;">​</a></h1><blockquote><p>Module: Module 4 · Transcendence Orthodox Definition Library | Benchmark base: Documents 03, 40, 29</p></blockquote><h2 id="introduction-laws-may-not-be-privately-modified-by-the-strong-—-this-is-heng-yuan-zhou-s-ultimate-negation-of-god-modifies-law" tabindex="-1">Introduction: laws may not be privately modified by the strong — this is Heng Yuan Zhou&#39;s ultimate negation of &quot;god-modifies-law&quot; <a class="header-anchor" href="#introduction-laws-may-not-be-privately-modified-by-the-strong-—-this-is-heng-yuan-zhou-s-ultimate-negation-of-god-modifies-law" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Introduction: laws may not be privately modified by the strong — this is Heng Yuan Zhou&#39;s ultimate negation of &quot;god-modifies-law&quot;&quot;">​</a></h2><p>One of the old system&#39;s greatest institutional loopholes is that laws may be modified at will by the strongest. The protagonist cultivates to the peak, feels a certain law is not handy, raises his hand and modifies it — this kind of writing reduces &quot;laws&quot; to the strong one&#39;s modeling clay. Heng Yuan Zhou jointly seals this loophole with the <strong>republican axiom of Myriad Races</strong> and the <strong>law-first axiom</strong>: laws may not be modified, but modifying laws must follow Myriad Ranks&#39; democratic procedure; no transcended one has the right to privately revise laws.</p><p>Six top-level axioms in this entry centrally embody the republican axiom of Myriad Races: law-revision right belongs to all Myriad Ranks; the transcended one is only the proposer and executor, not the legislator. The anti-predation axiom requires law revision not serve predators&#39; private gain; the collective ascension axiom requires revision&#39;s purpose be pushing the cosmos&#39; overall evolution; the causal self-discipline axiom requires the revision process be transparent to Myriad Ranks; the law-first axiom ensures the revision procedure itself is a law-level definition, which even transcended ones may not bypass to directly modify laws.</p><p>The universal equal infinite law: within the Anchor Symbiotic Civilization, all beings inherently possess basic infinite power; the easygoing retain a guaranteed basic infinity and will never be eliminated; strivers and Youth Supremes can superimpose more and higher levels of infinity. Infinite origin is inherent in all, so predation naturally loses its meaning.</p><p>This article focuses: how Heng Yuan Zhou&#39;s law-revision democratic procedure concretely operates.</p><h2 id="i-law-revision-s-scope-what-may-be-changed-what-may-not" tabindex="-1">I. Law Revision&#39;s Scope: What May Be Changed, What May Not <a class="header-anchor" href="#i-law-revision-s-scope-what-may-be-changed-what-may-not" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;I. Law Revision&#39;s Scope: What May Be Changed, What May Not&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Not all laws may be revised. Heng Yuan Zhou divides laws into two categories:</p><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>Law Category</th><th>Examples</th><th>May Be Revised</th><th>Revision Condition</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Fundamental laws</td><td>Energy conservation, anti-predation axiom, republican axiom of Myriad Races</td><td>Not revisable</td><td>No procedure may modify fundamental laws</td></tr><tr><td>Operating laws</td><td>Energy-transformation efficiency parameters, consciousness-domain interface standards, anchor-calibration frequency</td><td>Revisable</td><td>Follow complete democratic procedure</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Fundamental laws are Heng Yuan Zhou&#39;s &quot;constitution&quot;; they define the cosmos&#39; basic nature — energy conservation inviolable, anti-predation unshakable, Myriad-Rank equality inviolable. Once these laws are revised, the whole civilization&#39;s foundation shakes. Operating laws are the cosmos&#39; &quot;administrative regulations&quot;; they define concrete operational parameters and standards — these may be revised according to civilizational-development needs.</p><p>This distinction itself is the law-first axiom&#39;s embodiment: <strong>setting self-consistency above all — if fundamental laws may be casually changed, the setting is no longer self-consistent.</strong></p><h2 id="ii-law-revision-s-six-step-democratic-procedure" tabindex="-1">II. Law Revision&#39;s Six-Step Democratic Procedure <a class="header-anchor" href="#ii-law-revision-s-six-step-democratic-procedure" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;II. Law Revision&#39;s Six-Step Democratic Procedure&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Operating-law revision must follow a six-step democratic procedure:</p><ol><li><strong>Proposal initiation</strong>: any cultivator (not limited to transcended ones) may initiate a law-revision proposal. The proposal must explain revision reason, projected effect, impact scope.</li><li><strong>Myriad-Rank representative review</strong>: the proposal is submitted to the Myriad-Rank Republican Council, reviewed by each clan&#39;s representatives. Review focus: whether revision complies with fundamental laws, whether it benefits Myriad Ranks&#39; overall interest, whether hidden predatory risk exists.</li><li><strong>Quest Domain simulation review</strong>: the proposal is deduced in Quest Sediment Domain simulation review — if laws are revised per the proposal, what impact will it have on all cosmic layers? Deduction results serve as reference for Myriad-Rank representatives.</li><li><strong>Myriad-Rank referendum</strong>: after review passes, the proposal enters the Myriad-Rank referendum stage. Cultivators on planes and in races affected by the revision all have voting rights. Voting results are weighted by civilizational weight (see entry 706).</li><li><strong>Public notice and buffer period</strong>: after referendum passes, enter the public-notice period. During the notice period any cultivator may raise objections. After the notice period ends a buffer period is set, giving Myriad Ranks time to adapt to the coming law changes.</li><li><strong>Formal revision</strong>: after the buffer period ends, laws are formally revised. The revision process is executed by the transcended one — he is the technical operator of law revision, not the decision-maker.</li></ol><p>Six-step procedure&#39;s core logic: <strong>the transcended one revises laws, but does not legislate.</strong> What he executes is Myriad Ranks&#39; will, not his own.</p><h2 id="iii-the-transcended-one-s-role-in-the-revision-procedure" tabindex="-1">III. The Transcended One&#39;s Role in the Revision Procedure <a class="header-anchor" href="#iii-the-transcended-one-s-role-in-the-revision-procedure" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;III. The Transcended One&#39;s Role in the Revision Procedure&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The transcended one&#39;s role in law revision is very clear: <strong>technical executor</strong>, not political decision-maker. Concrete duties:</p><ul><li><strong>Proposal technical assessment</strong>: when a proposal involves law technical details, the transcended one is responsible for assessing the proposal&#39;s technical feasibility — whether the revision may be realized in the existing law network, how large the technical risk, what supporting engineering is needed;</li><li><strong>Simulation-review operation</strong>: Quest Sediment Domain simulation review&#39;s concrete operation is completed by the transcended one — he converts the proposal into a simulation model, runs the deduction, outputs a deduction report;</li><li><strong>Revision technical execution</strong>: after Myriad-Rank referendum passes, the transcended one executes concrete parameter revision in the law network — he is the law network&#39;s &quot;construction crew,&quot; not the &quot;design party&quot;;</li><li><strong>Post-revision monitoring</strong>: after revision completes, the transcended one continuously monitors the law network&#39;s operating state, confirming revision effects match the simulation deduction, reporting promptly when deviation appears.</li></ul><p>Four duties together: the transcended one is law-revision engineering&#39;s chief engineer — he understands technology, can operate, can monitor, but he does not decide &quot;whether to revise.&quot; &quot;Whether to revise&quot; is Myriad Ranks&#39; business.</p><h2 id="iv-why-a-democratic-procedure-is-necessary-historical-lessons-against-strong-ones-modifying-laws" tabindex="-1">IV. Why a Democratic Procedure Is Necessary: Historical Lessons Against &quot;Strong Ones Modifying Laws&quot; <a class="header-anchor" href="#iv-why-a-democratic-procedure-is-necessary-historical-lessons-against-strong-ones-modifying-laws" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;IV. Why a Democratic Procedure Is Necessary: Historical Lessons Against &quot;Strong Ones Modifying Laws&quot;&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Heng Yuan Zhou insists on the law-revision democratic procedure because the old system&#39;s historical lessons are too deep:</p><ul><li><strong>Consequence 1 of strong ones privately modifying laws: law collapse.</strong> In the old system, some strong one feels a certain law is not handy, raises his hand and modifies it — but the law he modified has deep connections with other laws; the change triggers a chain reaction, and the whole law network shows systematic collapse.</li><li><strong>Consequence 2: law bias.</strong> When strong ones modify laws, they inevitably favor themselves and their allies — the strong one&#39;s race benefits; other races are marginalized. This is the disease of &quot;legislators are the privileged class.&quot;</li><li><strong>Consequence 3: historical regression.</strong> When strong ones modify laws, they may write back the old era&#39;s predation-ism laws — because the strong one&#39;s interests do not align with Myriad Ranks&#39; interests.</li></ul><p>The democratic procedure institutionally prevents these three consequences: one more review step is one more layer of technical-risk gatekeeping; one more referendum step is one more layer of Myriad-Rank-interest guarantee; one more notice-buffer step is one more layer of historical-regression defense.</p><h2 id="v-five-core-takeaways" tabindex="-1">V. Five Core Takeaways <a class="header-anchor" href="#v-five-core-takeaways" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;V. Five Core Takeaways&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li><p><strong>Anti-energy waste</strong>: pre-revision simulation review avoids repeated waste of &quot;after revising find it wrong and change back&quot;; the public-notice buffer period avoids systematic disturbance caused by law mutation</p></li><li><p><strong>Anti-predation</strong>: the six-step procedure&#39;s Myriad-Rank representative review and referendum stages institutionally seal the channel of strong ones using law revision for private gain</p></li><li><p><strong>Tang-Luo upper-limit comparison</strong>: in the Tang-Luo system, strong ones modify laws whenever they want, no review no referendum; Heng Yuan Zhou&#39;s transcended one revising laws must follow a six-step democratic procedure; he is only the technical executor</p></li><li><p><strong>Myriad Races full coverage</strong>: referendum rights open to all Myriad-Rank races, all planes, all life forms; groups affected by the revision all have voting rights</p></li><li><p><strong>Hyper-multiverse full openness</strong>: the six-step procedure, fundamental vs. operating law classification, and the transcended one&#39;s technical role are all publicly queryable; Myriad Ranks may supervise the fairness of the revision procedure</p></li><li><p>Terminology alignment: the Balanced Anchor Hyper-Multiverse Realm is this batch&#39;s standard realm appellation; Alaya Network + multi-layer supervision monitors operation compliance throughout; the Myriad-Origin two-way cycle ensures energy and knowledge circulate perpetually among Myriad Ranks; exercise of law-anchor authority is strictly constrained by four-dimensional assessment and democratic procedure.</p></li><li><p><strong>Axiom 6 · Universal Equal Infinite Law</strong>: all beings inherently possess basic infinite power; the easygoing retain a guaranteed basic infinity and will not be eliminated by the times; strivers and Youth Supremes can superimpose more and higher levels of infinity — infinite origin inherent in all; predation naturally loses its meaning</p></li></ul><h2 id="conclusion" tabindex="-1">Conclusion <a class="header-anchor" href="#conclusion" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Conclusion&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The law-revision democratic procedure is the republican axiom of Myriad Races&#39; institutionalized fulfillment at the law dimension. It tells all cultivators: laws are not the strong one&#39;s modeling clay, but Myriad Ranks&#39; common contract. Fundamental laws may not be changed; operating laws may be changed but must follow procedure. The transcended one&#39;s role in it is chief engineer — he revises laws, but does not legislate; he operates, but does not decide. When law-revision right truly belongs to all Myriad Ranks, the law network will not be reduced to the strong one&#39;s private instrument, and civilization will not go into historical regression because of some strong one&#39;s personal will.</p><h2 id="related" tabindex="-1">Related <a class="header-anchor" href="#related" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Related&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li>Related documents: <a href="./../wanling-hengmao-origin-universe-archive/docs/zh/03-共生文明宪章.html">Entry 03 · Symbiotic-Civilization Charter</a> · <a href="./../wanling-hengmao-origin-universe-archive/docs/zh/40-共生宪法总纲.html">Entry 40 · Symbiotic Constitution Outline</a> · <a href="./../wanling-hengmao-origin-universe-archive/docs/zh/29-共生度评估体系.html">Entry 29 · Symbiosis-Degree Assessment System</a> · <a href="./../wanling-hengmao-origin-universe-archive/docs/zh/811_模块4-超脱者与法则-总论.html">Entry 811 · Transcended Ones and Laws Overview</a></li><li>Official site: <a href="https://faker210.github.io/hengyuan-cosmos/zh/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">https://faker210.github.io/hengyuan-cosmos/zh/</a></li></ul>',30)])])}const m=i(o,[["render",s]]);export{p as __pageData,m as default};
